    "https://esadefaculty.teamtailor.com/jobs/8641087-sustainability-management": {
      "title": "Sustainability Management",
      "description": "Sustainability Management - ESADE Faculty Positions Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. ESADE Faculty Positions and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics and marketing purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Marketing These cookies are used to make advertising messages more relevant to you. In some cases, they also deliver additional functions on the site. Vendors Youtube Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies esade.edu Society, Politics and Sustainability · Esade Barcelona - Sant Cugat Sustainability Management https://www.esade.edu/en Apply for this job The Department of Society, Politics and Sustainability at Esade Business School invites applications for a full-time, practitioner-track faculty position in Sustainability Management. Starting date: Fall, 2027. Candidates must have completed a PhD by the start date and must demonstrate a trajectory of at least 5 years in sustainability management in a company or organizational setting and have exposure to the challenges of sustainability adoption in firms. In addition, preferably, they will possess some research experience. Candidates must demonstrate experience or a clear teaching potential across our undergraduate, postgraduate and executive education programs. Profiles with a mixed trajectory in sustainability research and industry are especially encouraged to apply. We understand sustainability to include environmental, social and governance dimensions, and particularly their intersections. The position is for practitioner-track candidates, with a preference for early-career candidates, although we will also consider more experienced candidates. Decisions about contract renewal and promotion are based on teaching, research, service, outreach and work environment. We offer a competitive salary. The teaching load for this position is 200 hours. Almost all teaching and all official communications in the school are conducted in English. Knowledge of Spanish is not required, but for non-Spanish-speaking candidates language support is provided, if desired. The Department of Society, Politics and Sustainability at Esade is an active academic group, including professors teaching and doing research in Sociology, Business Ethics, Sustainability, Corporate Social Responsibility, Corporate Political Activity, Geopolitics, Social Entrepreneurship and Systems Thinking. The Department has close links with various European and US academic institutions and its members regularly participate in international research projects. Esade offers a rigorous and international academic environment for teaching and research. The school is home to faculty and students from all around the globe and is one of the leading business schools in international rankings. Esade comprises a Business School and a Law School spread across three campuses: Barcelona, Sant Cugat del Vallès (near Barcelona) and Madrid. The school’s mission includes providing a holistic education to individuals for them to become competent and socially responsible professionals; generating knowledge to help to improve organizations and society; and contributing to social debate and helping to build free, prosperous, fairer and socially and environmentally sustainable societies. Esade is also committed to continue increasing the diversity of its faculty. As an institution, Esade aims to bridge academia and practice, and facilitates close collaboration with companies, foundations and philanthropic organizations, public institutions and civil society through its institutes and chairs, and through applied research, partnerships and co-created projects. Faculty are encouraged to bring their professional networks into the classroom and to develop executive education programs, case studies and applied research with partner organizations. Its strong ties with the business community in Barcelona and Madrid, as well as a strong international alumni network and its role as a convener of public debate on business and society offer a unique platform for practitioners who want their experience to shape the next generation of responsible leaders and to have an impact beyond the classroom. Interested parties should send, through the application system: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement, which may focus on prospect evidence, knowledge generation, practice engagement and impact statement One recent publication or professional output Any available teaching evaluation The name and contact details of 3 referees (letters of recommendation will be requested only if the candidate is shortlisted) We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled but the search committee will begin reviewing applications on December 14, 2026. We expect to start conducting interviews shortly afterward. For any further queries about the application process, please contact marc.vilanova@esade.edu and include “[POSITIONS 2026]” in the subject. Department Society, Politics and Sustainability Location Esade Barcelona - Sant Cugat Apply for this job Society, Politics and Sustainability · Esade Barcelona - Sant Cugat Sustainability Management https://www.esade.edu/en Loading application form Close modal Start Jobs Data & privacy Manage cookies X Facebook LinkedIn Instagram esade.edu Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at ESADE Faculty Positions? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. @esade.edu Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
